1
00:03:51,428 --> 00:03:57,428
Your future is in its hands.

2
00:07:42,857 --> 00:07:48,857
The Terminator is a action, thriller, science
fiction film directed by James Cameron.

3
00:11:34,285 --> 00:11:40,285
In the post-apocalyptic future, reigning tyrannical supercomputers teleport a cyborg assassin known as the "Terminator" back to
1984 to kill Sarah Connor, whose unborn son is destined to lead insurgents against 21st century mechanical hegemony.

4
00:15:25,714 --> 00:15:31,714
Meanwhile, the human-resistance movement dispatches
a lone warrior to safeguard Sarah.

5
00:19:17,142 --> 00:19:23,142
Can he stop the virtually indestructible killing machine?

6
00:23:08,571 --> 00:23:14,571
Terminator, played by Arnold Schwarzenegger.

7
00:27:00,000 --> 00:27:06,000
Kyle Reese, played by Michael Biehn.

8
00:30:51,428 --> 00:30:57,428
Sarah Connor, played by Linda Hamilton.

9
00:34:42,857 --> 00:34:48,857
Traxler, played by Paul Winfield.

10
00:38:34,285 --> 00:38:40,285
Vukovich, played by Lance Henriksen.

11
00:42:25,714 --> 00:42:31,714
Matt, played by Rick Rossovich.

12
00:46:17,142 --> 00:46:23,142
The Terminator is a 1984 American science fiction action film directed by James
Cameron, written by Cameron and Gale Anne Hurd and produced by Hurd.

13
00:50:08,571 --> 00:50:14,571
It stars Arnold Schwarzenegger as the Terminator, a cybernetic assassin sent back in time from 2029 to 1984 to assassinate Sarah Connor (Linda Hamilton),
whose not-yet-conceived son will one day save mankind from extinction by Skynet, a hostile artificial intelligence, in a post-apocalyptic future.

14
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:06,000
Kyle Reese (Michael Biehn) is a soldier sent back in time to protect Sarah.

15
00:57:51,428 --> 00:57:57,428
The screenplay is credited to Cameron and Hurd,
while co-writer William Wisher Jr.

16
01:01:42,857 --> 01:01:48,857
received an "additional dialogue" credit.

17
01:05:34,285 --> 01:05:40,285
Cameron devised the premise of the film from a fever dream he experienced during the release of his first film,
Piranha II: The Spawning (1982), in Rome and developed the concept in collaboration with Wisher.

18
01:09:25,714 --> 01:09:31,714
He sold the rights to the project to fellow New World Pictures alumna Hurd on the condition that she would produce the film only if he were to direct it; Hurd eventually secured a distribution
deal with Orion Pictures, while executive producers John Daly and Derek Gibson of Hemdale Film Corporation were instrumental in setting up the film's financing and production.

19
01:13:17,142 --> 01:13:23,142
Originally approached by Orion for the role of Reese, Schwarzenegger
agreed to play the title character after befriending Cameron.

20
01:17:08,571 --> 01:17:14,571
Filming, which took place mostly at night on location in Los Angeles, was delayed because of Schwarzenegger's commitments to Conan the
Destroyer (1984), during which Cameron found time to work on the scripts for Rambo: First Blood Part II (1985) and Aliens (1986).

21
01:21:00,000 --> 01:21:06,000
The film's special effects, which included miniatures and stop-motion animation, were
created by a team of artists led by Stan Winston and Gene Warren Jr.

22
01:24:51,428 --> 01:24:57,428
Defying low pre-release expectations, The Terminator topped the United States box office for two
weeks, eventually grossing $78.3 million against a modest $6.4 million budget.

23
01:28:42,857 --> 01:28:48,857
It is credited with launching Cameron's film career and
solidifying Schwarzenegger's status as a leading man.

24
01:32:34,285 --> 01:32:40,285
The film's success led to a franchise consisting of several sequels, a
television series, comic books, novels and video games.

25
01:36:25,714 --> 01:36:31,714
In 2008, The Terminator was selected by the Library of Congress for
preservation in the United States National Film Registry.

26
01:40:17,142 --> 01:40:23,142
The film explores themes of man vs machine, artificial
intelligence (a.i.), saving the world, laser gun, cyborg.

27
01:44:08,571 --> 01:44:14,571
The tone is dark and thought_provoking and intense.
